✍️ OOP Concepts
    OOP refers to a type of computer programming in which programmers define not only data types but also the structure.

    Use this if interviewer asks OOP:
    OOP concepts like class, object, inheritance, encapsulation, polymorphism, and abstraction form the foundation of scalable software design.
    In my experience, OOP concepts are applied through architectural patterns like Clean Architecture and MVVM.
    Classes define structure,
    objects represent runtime data,
    inheritance helps reuse logic,
    encapsulation ensures controlled data access,
    polymorphism enables flexible behavior, and
    abstraction hides implementation details.
    Together, they help build maintainable, testable, and scalable applications.

