1) Class
-Class is a reference data type that follows a strict hierarchical relationship of superclass and subclass, with the class called
java.lang.Object as the root of class hierarchy.
-Class contains data members and member functions.
-Class also implements interfaces and extends abstract classes.

🌍 Real-World Example
    Bank Account Blueprint
    Fields: accountNumber, balance
    Functions: deposit(), withdraw()

    data class BankAccount(
        val accountNumber: String,
        var balance: Double
    ) {
        fun deposit(amount: Double) {
            balance += amount
        }

        fun withdraw(amount: Double) {
            balance -= amount
        }
    }

