4) Encapsulation
-Data encapsulation is process of packing/wrapping data members and member function in a single unit called class or object.
-A Java class is the example of encapsulation.
-JavaBean model is fully encapsulated class because all data members are private.

🌍 Real-World Example
    Bank Account
        You cannot directly access balance
        Only via deposit/withdraw

   class BankAccount(private var balance: Double) {
       fun deposit(amount: Double) {
           balance += amount
       }
       fun getBalance(): Double {
           return balance
       }
   }

