6)Abstraction:
-Abstraction is the process of just declaring the functionality not define in details.
-Can be achieve by using the concept of abstract class.
🌍 Real-World Example
Abstract Class	BankAccount (defines that every account must be able to deposit and withdraw, but doesn't specify how yet).
Abstract Method	calculateInterest() (every account has interest, but a "Savings Account" calculates it differently than a "Current Account").
Concrete Class	SavingsAccount or CurrentAccount (where the "details" are finally defined).

